      "content": "but i don't have my glucometer on me right now and the doctor's office is closed. i really don't want to risk it going too high and getting ketoacidosis or something. if i just take one single unit of my rapid-acting insulin it should be fine to level me out, right? it's just one unit, it's not like it's a huge dose.",
